BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Local Author Steve Allen Presentation
DTSTART;TZID=MST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260210T180000
DTEND;TZID=MST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260210T200000
UID:cf9836eb16355d673ef0de3380feaaf7@backofbeyondbooks.com
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, February 10th ~ 6 pm\nHistorian Steve Allen will pre
 sent a slide show covering his many years of exploring the canyon country 
 of Southern Utah. Topics include his family’s history of desert explorat
 ion\; a discussion of threats to the land\, thoughts about the ongoing bat
 tles of land protection in Utah\, and stories centered on “History on th
 e Ground- Pieces of the Puzzle.”\nSteve Allen is a widely recognized exp
 ert on the history and pre-history of the canyonlands of Southern Utah. 
 His guide books are considered the “go to” sources for accurate inform
 ation. Steve’s Utah’s Canyon Country Place Names is a comprehensive an
 d exhaustive two-volume reference work that helps tell the stories of the 
 pioneers who put names on the land. Steve spends eight months a year backp
 acking and has a home in Durango\, Colorado.
LOCATION:Star Hall\, 159 E Center St\, Moab\, UT 84532
URL:https://backofbeyondbooks.com/happenings/local-author-steve-allen-pres
 entation-tuesday-february-10th-6-pm-star-hall/
X-SOURCE:Back of Beyond Books
END:VEVENT
